  }))), "Health"), mdx("p", null, "I ran 950 km this year. After switching into a heavy-work mode near the end of the year, I kept strength training consistently, but I didn\u2019t have the psychological slack to run. Running has a higher \u201Ccost.\u201D But I didn\u2019t set a goal for how many kilometers I \u201Cshould\u201D run anyway. Next year I\u2019ll run whenever I feel like it\u2014and in April, I\u2019m running a half marathon."), mdx("p", null, "I want to go out at night and also study personally, but once I work out after work, the day is just over, and I can\u2019t stand that. So I tried to make morning workouts a habit. After fighting myself desperately for about half a year, it became a bit easier to shake off that cosmic force of not wanting to exercise immediately after waking up. This might be the biggest gain of the year. I either run 8 km in the morning or do strength training at a gym near the office."), mdx("p", null, "My herniated disc improved a lot, thankfully. I caught a few colds. Maybe because I\u2019m getting older, my body feels a bit drier. Next year, I want to make meditation a routine too. I still hate hospitals so, so much, but I want to get better at going."), mdx("h1", {
