  }))), "Finance"), mdx("p", null, "I spent some money on traveling, but I succeeded in cutting spending quite a bit compared to last year. Part of it was trying not to buy many things. Also, I\u2019ve been living in my current home for well over three years now, so there isn\u2019t much I particularly want or need anymore."), mdx("p", null, "I improved the constitution and weightings of my portfolio a lot, so compared to last year, I built an environment where I can invest with relatively more peace of mind. At the same time, I raised my equity allocation a lot and greatly increased the amount per buy in a single name. I truly felt how important cash is, and I think I\u2019ll keep thinking deeply about how not to dismantle my investment allocation when large expenses arise. I say the same thing every year at year-end. \u201CI was satisfied with my investment return this year. Next year I have no confidence, and I\u2019m worried about the market situation, so I still don\u2019t know what strategy to take. I want to invest with a bit more peace of mind, but it really isn\u2019t easy.\u201D"), mdx("p", null, "I want to study real estate a bit. People around me bought homes occasionally this year. I\u2019m living pretty roughly right now, but housing is something you can\u2019t avoid forever. There\u2019s probably value in knowing certain things in advance."), mdx("h1", {
