  }))), "Life"), mdx("p", null, "It was a year spent almost entirely together with my partner. I tried really hard to have fun on weekends. We went around a lot together. We spent the most time in Sindang, Jamsil, and Seokchon, and also enjoyed Yongsan, Haebangchon, Yeonnam, Hannam, Yaksu, Geumho, Seongsu, Seoul Forest, Konkuk Univ., Anguk, Seochon, and Maebong. We went to Cigarettes After Sex and Coldplay concerts together, looked at a lot of furniture in showrooms, drank about six bottles of wine together, and ate a lot of peaches, tangerines, strawberries, mochi bread, Shine Muscat, and Lalasweet pint ice cream. Hanging out with my partner was explosively fun, to the point where I once came back from a developer coffee chat and rambled about how insanely funny and awesome my partner is\u2014how can someone be like that\u2026"), mdx("p", null, "I took three domestic trips. During a two-week refresh vacation, I walked 160 km along the East Coast over 10 days. The difficulty was lower than I expected, so next time I think I should aim for about 20 km a day. I\u2019ll probably keep doing a bit each year toward the goal of completing the Haeparang Trail. I already planned everything for this year too. Since I don\u2019t travel that much, I didn\u2019t really have a \u201Ctaste\u201D for it, but I realized I like trying to deeply understand the humanistic environment and subtle points of the places I travel to. I like learning that Yangnam-myeon in Gyeongju is a National Geopark, understanding what kind of volcanic activity created columnar joints, and why there are so many volcanic landforms along Korea\u2019s East Coast. Compared to going to somewhere like Europe once in a while, I think it\u2019s much more fun to visit places or countries with some shared \u201Chomogeneity\u201D multiple times."), mdx("p", null, "I did so, so many things that by year-end I was completely in a groggy state. And then I got put into a busy project at work, so from the start of 4Q until now I\u2019ve been working 50+ hours a week. While reflecting that maybe I became a bit cynical from being tired, I also learned that after getting tired this time, I\u2019ve built a certain mental resilience to these situations. I\u2019ll keep trying to maintain high intensity and density at work while still making efforts to have fun."), mdx("p", null, "I\u2019m moving next year. I\u2019ve lived alone for 10 years, and I decided to stop doing that. It\u2019s an enormous decision in my life."), mdx("h1", {
